 <!-- Append new entries below; newest first. -->
 
+### #17 — Event-timer wheel: static slot table + generation handles (2026-09-16)
+- **Learned:** (1) An armed-but-never-serviced timer is a silent liveness hole: with the tick hook BSP-only (AP early-return), arm() must fail closed for cpu != 0 — caught by audit iter-1 S2, not by tests (unit tests happily tick any cpu). (2) Test expiry bases must derive from the LIVE clock: a fixed synthetic base below the suite-position clock makes timers born-expired and turns asserts into ISR timing luck (flaked at position 1318 in `all` while green standalone; fixed via ns_monotonic()+10s). (3) Auditor corrective patches can be corrupt/hallucinated line numbers — always `git apply --check` first, then implement manually per findings; the S2 intent still applied verbatim. (4) New top-level kernel dirs need no mk changes (SRC find auto-globs) but DO need gen.mk regen per arch like any new .cpp. (5) `pending_patch.diff` regenerated post-staging via `git diff HEAD` excluding itself; new-file coverage needs `git add -N` first with a `grep -c '^diff --git'` count check.
+- **Adapted:** src/kernel/time/timer_wheel.{hpp,cpp} (IrqSpinLockGuard arm/cancel, try-lock-skip + earliest-8 + unlock-before-fire on_tick, snapshot_reset with generation bump), Scheduler::on_tick hook position (after DeadlineList scan, before alarms) + callback contract comment, test_timer_wheel.cpp (8 deterministic tests, live-based expiries); audits/report-20260916-134406.md (APPROVED iter-2).
+- **Style re-surface:** CODING_STYLE §11 (no spinlock across reschedule — wheel never reschedules; IrqSpinLockGuard short sections; ISR try-lock-skip per TlbShootdown precedent), §12.2 (generation-tagged handles, kInvalidGeneration skip, LIFO-reuse test), §5 (fail-closed arm/cancel/BSPreject, ENSURE-free), §7 test-first (stubs green before impl, history row per run).
+
 ### #16 — HRT monotonic clock: TickSource + ns_monotonic + oneshot/remaining (2026-09-16)
 - **Learned:** (1) x86_64 `Timer::oneshot/periodic/remaining` were declared but never defined — linkable only because nothing referenced them (`test_hal` stubs document the gap); filling them is additive but their LAPIC delegation steals the system tick, so tests must steal-and-restore via the `apic_timer_oneshot` re-init pattern before further asserts. (2) `mk/cpp-rules.*.gen.mk` (arch-specific ones are git-ignored) regenerate only when `mk/rules.mk`/`Makefile` change — every new `.cpp` needs `rm mk/cpp-rules.<arch>.gen.mk` before building, for each arch. (3) Cross-arch compile can be verified per-TU with `-fsyntax-only` + the exact per-arch flags when full cross builds die on a pre-existing unrelated error (here `tlb_shootdown` on baseline, confirmed via `stash -u` + rebuild). (4) `calibrate()` idempotency needs the label refresh separated from the frequency work: APIC CPUID caps probe after `Timer::init`, so a cached TSC label must promote to TSC_DEADLINE on repeat calls.
 - **Adapted:** `arch::Timer::resolve_source` (preference chain TSC→HPET→PIT, `CONFIG_HRT_*` knobs), `detail::monotonic_commit` CAS clamp (atomics-only `last_ns_`), overflow-split tick/ns/TSC conversions (1 h clamp), fail-closed `hpet::probe` (no MMIO touch until ACPI/VMM mapping lands); audits/report-20260916-130230.md (APPROVED, 3x S3 carried to #17: plain `active_source_` access, HPET stub, LAPIC steal-and-restore contract).
